{
  "_comment_paths": "start_url, scope and every icon src are RELATIVE. A manifest's relative URLs resolve against the manifest's own URL (/blackjack/manifest.webmanifest), so they land on /blackjack/ with no build-time substitution. Absolute paths would have to be kept in step with Vite's `base` by hand, and the failure is silent: the app still installs, but launches to the wrong scope.",
  "_comment_no_sw": "There is deliberately NO service worker anywhere in this app, so it will not launch with no network at all — even though a game against the cats needs no server once loaded. That is the trade the other games made too: a site redeployed this often is far more likely to strand a player on a stale cached bundle than to be opened offline. Home-screen install, standalone display and the icons all work without one.",
  "name": "Blackjack",
  "short_name": "Blackjack",
  "description": "Blackjack with no sign-up: up to seven computer cats at your table, or share a room code and play up to eight friends online.",
  "start_url": "./",
  "scope": "./",
  "display": "standalone",
  "orientation": "portrait",
  "theme_color": "#24160d",
  "background_color": "#24160d",
  "categories": ["games"],

  "_comment_links": "Same reasoning as yahtzee: when someone with the app installed opens an invite link (/blackjack/join/ABCDE), 'handle_links: preferred' routes it INTO the installed app and 'navigate-existing' reuses the open window instead of starting a second copy with a second set of listeners on the room. Chromium-only; iOS ignores both, which is why the shared message also carries the code as text.",
  "handle_links": "preferred",
  "launch_handler": {
    "client_mode": "navigate-existing"
  },

  "icons": [
    {
      "_comment": "An Ace, a King and a cat's paw on green felt (icon.svg). Full-bleed, so it also works masked.",
      "src": "icons/icon-192.png",
      "sizes": "192x192",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "any"
    },
    {
      "src": "icons/icon-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "any"
    },
    {
      "_comment": "purpose 'maskable' — Android crops these to the launcher's shape. The cards and paw sit inside the middle 80% safe zone, so the same files serve. Listed as separate entries rather than 'any maskable' on one icon, which makes the platform pick one interpretation.",
      "src": "icons/icon-192.png",
      "sizes": "192x192",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "maskable"
    },
    {
      "src": "icons/icon-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "maskable"
    }
  ]
}
